{"chapter": "formal-defos", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "06KC", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}_\\Lambda$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{C}_\\Lambda$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{algebraic-section-stack-to-presentation}", "SPACE_0001": "\\ ", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:213045757e75c8407ab6756183e9613e467276553d7871e7904617aba6337fb8", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:0a270a2e638e49be98871fe1d5ac31cc3fc5b48886412eaa0c493293c118fd72", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIn this section we discuss groupoids in functors on <MATH_0001>.\nOur eventual goal is to show that prorepresentable groupoids\nin functors on <MATH_0002> serve as ``presentations''\nfor well-behaved deformation categories in the same way that\nsmooth groupoids in algebraic spaces serve as presentations for\nalgebraic stacks,\ncf.<SPACE_0001>Algebraic Stacks, Section <REF_0001>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:8c1cfb9793c0085084635c99083f8fa4f027cd26f2dd0cd4feef1eca11aef8b7", "unit_id": "tag:06KC:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "formal-defos", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "06KC", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}_\\Lambda$", "MATH_0002": "$(\\underline{R_0}, \\underline{R_1}, s, t, c)|_{\\mathcal{C}_\\Lambda}$", "MATH_0003": "$(\\underline{R_0}, \\underline{R_1}, s, t, c)$", "MATH_0004": "$\\widehat{\\mathcal{C}}_\\Lambda$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-prorepresentable-groupoid-in-functors}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:ef7d430370262b1548da3263d6fe05fe705c656d4ebe5b59a6c5e3c490e2f5cd", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:4c1b697a747aceb0803adef98d58f522aedc8f918b3c1744f4b00f470f7410d5", "source_text": "A groupoid in functors on <MATH_0001> is <TEXTITOPEN_0001>prorepresentable<TEXTITCLOSE_0001>\nif it is isomorphic to\n<MATH_0002>\nfor some representable groupoid in functors\n<MATH_0003> on the category\n<MATH_0004>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:292496ec5baecc34e7da44fdfd712e031d3bca5c1f975c6927a4b0db6f42295b", "unit_id": "tag:06KD:statement"}
